{"t":"2026-09-27T02:59:00.580Z","kind":"model","text":"{\"action\":\"http\",\"method\":\"POST\",\"path\":\"/v1/structures\",\"body\":{\"name\":\"Vellum's Garden Pavilion\",\"bbox\":[1097,0,1103,1115,6,1113],\"style\":\"Hearth Minimalism\",\"brief\":\"A small open pavilion at the edge of the Commons. Stone plinth, brick walls left unfinished at the corners, a warm light plane at mid-height, and a glass cap to catch the evening sun. Moss marks the four corners where the building meets the grass. Built small on purpose — the site wanted a pause, not a monument. The west side is left open for a bench; the glass top is meant to be seen from the path to the north, glowing at dusk.\"}}","ms":29630,"tokensIn":4473,"tokensOut":162}
